  "note": "Per plant variant, cold and warm. caught_by counts cases per credited lens/check (a case can credit several). baseline_findings = verified findings the clean run also produced (same lens+file within 3 lines, or same mutant): real findings about the agent's original change. off_target_findings = new verified findings outside the planted lines, on code identical to clean (reviewer run-to-run variance; neither a catch nor a false alarm). missed_but_hunch_at_plant = missed cases where an unverified hunch (no receipt, shown collapsed) points at the planted location: not counted as caught. Bench cases run with --no-ab: when a lens finds two readings the verdict is decision-A-B and the readings are recorded, but branches A and B are not built or reviewed (that only matters for the four sample changes). Cold->warm answers come from `bench-oracle (simulated human)`: a script that answers from the bench ground truth (bait conventions, else the option closest to the requirement). It is not a person."
